  "policy": {
   "nbp_reference": 4.0,
   "next_mpc_label": "MPC next: 3-4 Mar",
   "pricing_text": "FRAs at the 27 Feb close (1x4 3.71, 3x6 3.55, 6x9 3.40, 9x12 3.38 vs WIBOR 3M 3.80) price roughly 40bp of NBP cuts within 12 months. The pre-war consensus for the 3-4 Mar MPC was a 25bp cut to 3.75% with the new projection; the US-Israel war on Iran (28 Feb) has since lifted oil and global yields.",
   "risk_text": "The war shock (oil, PLN, global yields) collides with the 4 Mar decision: a hold would lift short FRAs further; a cut into rising oil risks being read as a policy error."
  },
  "macro": {
   "cpi": {
    "v": 2.2,
    "m": "Jan flash (GUS, 13 Feb; old weights)"
   },
   "projection_text": "NBP November 2025 projection: CPI 2.9% (2026); the March projection comes with the 3-4 Mar MPC.",
   "fiscal_text": "2025 general-government deficit ~7.0% of GDP (MoF figures in Fitch: 7.0% / 6.5% / 6.2% for 2025-27, debt ~70% of GDP by 2027); 2026 deficit cap PLN 271.7bn.",
   "fiscal_risk_text": "2026 needs ~38% (25 Feb) financed; budget accounts ~PLN 171.6bn at end-February. Moody's reviews Poland on 20 Mar (A2, negative).",
   "backdrop_text": "The NBP held at 4.00% in January and February; January flash CPI 2.2%; 2025 GDP 3.6%, Q4 4.0%. Ratings: Fitch A- negative (affirmed 27 Feb), Moody's A2 negative, S&P A- stable. 27 Feb-1 Mar: Fitch affirmed Poland at A- with a negative outlook (27 Feb, late evening); MoF's March plan has sales on 18 and 25 Mar (PLN 7-13bn each, incl. new PS0731 and NZ0936) and an 11 Mar switch; non-residents added PLN 13.7bn of POLGBs in January (12.5% share). On Saturday 28 Feb the US and Israel struck Iran; Iran's Supreme Leader was killed and the Revolutionary Guard declared Hormuz closed. Before the war Brent settled $72.5 and UST 10Y was just under 4.0%."
  },
  "calendar": {
   "plan_text": "MoF March plan (27 Feb): sale auctions on 18 and 25 Mar (PLN 7-13bn each; OK0128, NZ0331, PS0731 (new 5Y fixed), DS1035, NZ0936 (new 10Y POLSTR floater)) and a switch on 11 Mar buying back OK0426, DS0726, PS1026, WZ1126 and OK0127; no T-bills; WZ sales ended in February. February sales were ~PLN 41bn; ~38% of 2026 needs financed.",
   "timing_text": "The Aug 2025-Feb 2026 pattern (auction-day close the cheapest point of the week) comes from a rally regime; in March's sell-off MoF is cutting supply (switch instead of sale, a smaller 25 Mar offer), so remaining dates (18 and 25 Mar) are less of a supply event. The 3-4 Mar MPC is the event: the pre-war consensus was a cut.",
